      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Carotid stump syndrome is a well-documented embolic source for ischemic stroke. However, few cases have been reported of a similar condition-termed vertebral artery stump syndrome-which affects the posterior circulation after vertebral artery origin occlusion. We herein report a case of infarction of the right superior cerebellar artery and left posterior inferior cerebellar artery territories due to vertebral artery stump syndrome. In this interesting case, a turbulent flow at the distal side of the vertebral artery occlusion was captured on ultrasonography, and was identified as the probable mechanism of vertebral artery stump syndrome."},
